    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full `mvn test` build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner create so that the value is stripped of non-digits and required to be exactly 10 digits.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the strict `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'` on `OwnerFields.telephone`. That pattern rejected formatted input (e.g. `(04) 1234-5678`) during DTO bean-validation *before* normalization could run, which would have made it a 400 for valid-but-formatted numbers. `minLength`/`maxLength` are kept.\n\n2. **`BuildOwner.java`** (`POST /api/owners` pipeline) \u2014 After the existing required-field check, it normalizes the telephone with `replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`, requires exactly 10 digits, and stores the normalized value back on the request before mapping to the `Owner` entity. If it isn't exactly 10 digits after stripping, it throws the new checked `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n3. **`InvalidTelephoneException.java`** + **`InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`** + **escalation YAML** \u2014 New checked exception and its OfficeFloor escalation handler that responds `400 Bad Request` with a ProblemDetail (mirroring the existing `MissingOwnerFields` pattern).\n\n**Behavior:**\n- `(04) 1234-5678` \u2192 normalized to `0412345678`, stored/returned as `telephone` (test `coreStripsToTenDigits` passes).\n- `12345` \u2192 5 digits after stripping \u2192 `400` (test `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` passes).\n- The stored 10-digit value also satisfies the existing `Owner` entity `@Pattern`/`@Digits` constraints on save.\n\n`mvn test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
